goodfoot's instructions, skillify, and documentation templates address their reader through the `it.hostAgentName` accessor over the verified per-platform `hostAgentName` fact, which stays separate from `hostIdentity` because a template needs its reader's name even where the host injects no identity sentence; the portability lint matches only conventions filenames, worktree tool names, and plugin-root variables — never a bare agent name — and no check renders these templates, so a template that hardcodes one agent's name silently ships it into the other three platforms' rendered trees.
